*.plugin.zip

# Loose smoke-test screenshots dropped at the repo root by agent-browser runs.
# Persisted captures belong under docs/ or marketing/assets/, not the root.
/*.png

# AI coding-tool scratch/config dirs — local tooling, never source
.factory/
.trae/
.windsurf/
.gstack/
.playwright-mcp/
.turbo/
# Per-project Studio sidecars. `**/` is load-bearing: every real `.studio/`
# lives at `studio-workspace/<project>/.studio/`, and a pattern containing a
# slash is anchored to THIS file's directory — so the bare `.studio/…` forms
# these replace matched only a root-level dir that never exists, silently
# leaving every one of these files tracked.
**/.studio/daemon.json
**/.studio/vite/
# Install-job durability sidecar: per-machine operational state (absolute app-root
# path + pid of the process that spawned the install), rewritten on every install.
# Same class as daemon.json above — it must survive a server restart, not a clone.
**/.studio/install-job.json
# Compiled-style cache: `styles-<hash>.{css,json}`, keyed on a content hash of
# the inputs (server/handlers/studio/styleCompile.ts). Pure derived output —
# regenerated on demand, and committing it only produces churn in every diff.
**/.studio/cache/
# Design references (server/handlers/studio/designReferenceStore.ts) —
# durable, addressable-by-id copies of a design comp (typically a Figma
# export) an agent measures a Studio frame against. Unlike every OTHER entry
# in this section, these are NOT disposable/regenerable output — losing one
# means the user has to re-supply the exact file. They are excluded anyway,
# for a different reason: a multi-megabyte PNG is a real, ongoing cost to
# carry in a git history, and this repo's own studio-workspace/* dev fixtures
# would otherwise accumulate them on every session that exercises this
# feature. Durability here means "survives across chat turns/restarts on the
# running server's disk", not "survives a git clone" — see the store's own
# module doc for the full reasoning.
**/.studio/references/
# Design variables (server/handlers/studio/designVariableStore.ts) — an
# ingested design's OWN declared variable table (typically read by the agent
# via a connected Figma MCP server's get_variable_defs and handed to Studio
# to persist), so studio_measure_reference can answer a measurement by
# lookup instead of pixel inference. Same durability class and exclusion
# reasoning as .studio/references/ just above: user-supplied intent, not
# disposable, but cheap enough to lose that "survives on the running
# server's disk" is the durability guarantee, not "survives a git clone" —
# the agent re-fetches it from the design tool on request.
**/.studio/variables/

# --- studio-workspace/ -- USER DATA, not this repository's source -----------
# STUDIO-FIGMA-FEEL-PLAN.md §6 decision 4. Every `studio-workspace/<project>/`
# is a user's own React repository checked out inside this one, so the default
# is IGNORED: a dogfooding session, a GitHub import, or a bench fixture
# (`__bench-synth/` and `__bench-live-synth/`, whose one-by-one rules this
# blanket rule replaces) must never turn up in `git status` as something to
# commit. The missing rule cost 140,894 committed lines in `188fda1a`.
#
# The negations below are the named sample projects this repo's own tests open.
# Adding one means committing someone's repository into this one, so the list
# stays short and every entry names its consumer:
#
#   __canonical-fixture/  src/core/page-parser/__tests__/canonicalCheck.test.ts
#                         server/handlers/studio/canonicalPageCheck.test.ts
#                         server/handlers/studio/pageSourceFile.test.ts
#                         scripts/bench/benches/agent-turn.ts
#   test4/                the Phase 0 dogfood target (plan §3) and the project
#                         `PropertiesPanel/imageFillValue.ts` documents against
#
# `test4 copy/` is deliberately NOT kept -- it is a local dogfooding duplicate,
# and `scripts/bench/lib/liveFrameFixture.ts` degrades with a named error when
# it is absent. The e2e specs' own projects (`maherfayad-stack-eSIM`,
# `esim-journey`) are not kept either: each spec `test.skip`s when its project
# is not on disk, which is the intended contract for real user data.
studio-workspace/*
!studio-workspace/.ignore
!studio-workspace/__canonical-fixture/
!studio-workspace/test4/

# Inside a kept sample project, that project's OWN generated output is still
# ignored. `prototype/*.generated.*` is re-emitted by the prototype connector
# on every scan (`server/handlers/studio/prototypeRoutes.ts`) -- 64k lines for
# `test4` alone, rewritten on every dogfood. `node_modules/` and `dist/` need
# no entry here: the root rules at the top of this file already match at any
# depth (and `studio-workspace/.ignore` re-includes them for ripgrep only).
studio-workspace/*/prototype/*.generated.*

# The per-project guide Studio writes into a kept sample project on every chat
# turn (`server/handlers/studio/projectGuide.ts`, tracked by
# `.claude/.studio-generated.json`). Generated output, not source — distinct
# from THIS repo's own `.claude/` harness and root `CLAUDE.md`, both tracked
# above. In a user's OWN project these files are theirs to commit; here they
# are regenerated dev-fixture noise.
studio-workspace/*/.claude/
studio-workspace/*/CLAUDE.md

# Playwright/E2E run output — generated, not source
test-results/

# The Vite prototype shell `ensurePrototypeShell` scaffolds into a project.
# Generated output, rewritten on demand — and, inside `__canonical-fixture/`,
# a real hazard: that directory is BOTH a Studio project and the parser
# suite's committed reference corpus, and the `prototypeShellBoards`-family
# tests scaffold onto the checked-in copy rather than a tmp copy (the
# `live-01` landmine in STATE.md). Without these rules one full `bun test`
# leaves ~15 generated files inside the fixture and the next `git add` sweeps
# them into the corpus — which is exactly what happened while this rule was
# being written. Scoped to the fixture: a USER's project owns its own shell.
studio-workspace/__canonical-fixture/prototype/
studio-workspace/__canonical-fixture/index.html
studio-workspace/__canonical-fixture/vite.config.js
studio-workspace/__canonical-fixture/.studio/shell.json
